{"step_index":2283,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-27T05:15:44Z","thinking":"The HTML `<title>` tag for the renderer is identified as \"pmodule.\" The executable name is the Braille blank space character. Observing how Windows Task Manager labels Electron apps, the group name is derived from the executable name or `FileDescription` from PE headers. Given the executable name is `⠀.exe` and `FileDescription` likely also appears as `⠀`.\n\n\nWindows Task Manager labels Electron apps according to the executable name and window title. The user wants the application to appear as `⠀` and `pmodule` in Task Manager, mirroring the observed Parakeet application. Achieving this requires renaming the Electron executable to the Braille blank space and setting the HTML title to \"pmodule.\" A direct launch method (shortcut or VBScript) will prevent a visible console window.\n\nTo ensure Parakeet's prints capture the application, the printing configuration must be checked and likely modified to include the intended window or application instance.\n\n\nThe application's disappearance in screenshots is likely due to capture protection features. Specifically, the observed behavior suggests the use of a function that excludes the window from being captured.\n\nA potential solution involves modifying the window's properties using a single command. Executing this command would disable the capture protection, making the application visible in screenshots. Alternatively, a simpler approach could be capturing the screen with a cell phone.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"$code = @\"\nusing System;\nusing System.Text;\nusing System.Runtime.InteropServices;\nusing System.Collections.Generic;\nusing System.Diagnostics;\n\npublic class AffinityFixer {\n    public delegate bool EnumWindowsProc(IntPtr hWnd, IntPtr lParam);\n\n    [DllImport(\"user32.dll\")]\n    public static extern bool EnumWindows(EnumWindowsProc enumProc, IntPtr lParam);\n\n    [DllImport(\"user32.dll\")]\n    public static extern uint GetWindowThreadProcessId(IntPtr hWnd, out uint lpdwProcessId);\n\n    [DllImport(\"user32.dll\", SetLastError = true)]\n    public static extern bool SetWindowDisplayAffinity(IntPtr hWnd, uint dwAffinity);\n\n    [DllImport(\"user32.dll\", SetLastError = true)]\n    public static extern bool GetWindowDisplayAffinity(IntPtr hWnd, out uint dwAffinity);\n\n    public static List<string> MakeParakeetVisible() {\n        var results = new List<string>();\n        var pids = new HashSet<uint>();\n        foreach (var p in Process.GetProcesses()) {\n            try {\n                if (p.MainModule.FileName.Contains(\"parakeetai-desktop\")) {\n                    pids.Add((uint)p.Id);\n                }\n            } catch {}\n        }\n\n        EnumWindows((hWnd, lParam) => {\n            uint pid;\n            GetWindowThreadProcessId(hWnd, out pid);\n            if (pids.Contains(pid)) {\n                uint currentAffinity;\n                if (GetWindowDisplayAffinity(hWnd, out currentAffinity)) {\n                    bool success = SetWindowDisplayAffinity(hWnd, 0); // 0 = WDA_NONE\n                    results.Add(string.Format(\"HWND: {0} | Prev Affinity: {1} | Set to 0: {2}\", hWnd, currentAffinity, success));\n                }\n            }\n            return true;\n        }, IntPtr.Zero);\n\n        return results;\n    }\n}\n\"@\nAdd-Type -TypeDefinition $code -Language CSharp\n[AffinityFixer]::MakeParakeetVisible()","Cwd":"c:\\Users\\Arthur Henrique\\Documents\\GitHub\\Spectra","WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolAction":"Testing removing display affinity from Parakeet windows","toolSummary":"Test SetWindowDisplayAffinity 0"}}]}
